e it really well.", "Before an adverb"], ["오늘 진짜 피곤해요.", "I am really tired today.", "Expressing strong feeling"]], "nuance": "A casual, friendly word for really, slightly less formal than jeongmal in tone.", "mistakes": ["Do not use it in very formal writing."]}, {"kind": "adverb", "hangul": "잘", "english": "well", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": [], "usage": [["잘 자요.", "Sleep well.", "Before a verb"], ["한국어를 잘해요.", "I speak Korean well.", "Attaches before haeyo"], ["잘 들어요.", "I hear it well.", "Shows good ability"], ["잘 먹어요.", "I eat well.", "Common daily phrase"]], "examples": [["그 사람은 노래를 잘해요.", "That person sings well.", "Showing a skill"], ["저는 운동을 잘 못해요.", "I cannot exercise well.", "Used with negative"], ["오늘 잘 지냈어요.", "I spent the day well.", "Before a verb"]], "nuance": "Describes doing something skillfully or in a good state, placed right before the verb.", "mistakes": ["Do not use it before an adjective."]}, {"kind": "adverb", "hangul": "더", "english": "more", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": [], "usage": [["더 주세요.", "Please give me more.", "Before a verb"], ["더 커요.", "It is bigger.", "Marks the comparison"], ["더 좋아요.", "It is better.", "Before an adjective"], ["더 빨라요.", "It is faster.", "Compares two things"]], "examples": [["이 가방이 더 비싸요.", "This bag is more expensive.", "Comparing two items"], ["조금 더 먹고 싶어요.", "I want to eat a bit more.", "Before a verb"], ["오늘이 어제보다 더 더워요.", "Today is hotter than yesterday.", "Used with boda"]], "nuance": "Marks a greater degree or amount, the basic way to make comparisons in Korean.", "mistakes": ["Do not drop it when comparing things."]}, {"kind": "adverb", "hangul": "덜", "english": "less", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": [], "usage": [["덜 매워요.", "It is less spicy.", "Before an adjective"], ["덜 자요.", "I sleep less.", "Before a verb"], ["덜 추워요.", "It is less cold.", "Opposite of deo"], ["덜 바빠요.", "I am less busy.",